---
// Worked example for the "Depreciation Recapture" section of the capital gains Insights post:
// how depreciation lowers basis, and how the sale price splits into basis returned, recaptured
// depreciation (up to 25% federal) and price growth (0/15/20% federal). Round numbers on purpose.
---

<figure class="recapture">
	<figcaption class="recapture__title">Example: A Building Bought for $1,000,000 and Sold for $2,000,000</figcaption>

	<ol class="recapture__steps">
		<li>
			<span class="recapture__step-label">1. You bought the building</span>
			<span class="recapture__step-value">$1,000,000</span>
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="recapture__step-label">2. Over the years, you deducted depreciation</span>
			<span class="recapture__step-value recapture__step-value--gold">&minus;$400,000</span>
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="recapture__step-label">3. So your "tax cost" (adjusted basis) is now</span>
			<span class="recapture__step-value">$600,000</span>
		</li>
	</ol>

	<p class="recapture__bar-label">You sell for $2,000,000 (after selling costs). Here is how the IRS splits that up:</p>

	<div
		class="recapture__bar"
		role="img"
		aria-label="Of the $2,000,000 sale price, $600,000 is your adjusted basis returned and not taxed, $400,000 is depreciation recapture taxed at up to 25% federally, and $1,000,000 is price growth taxed at 0%, 15%, or 20% federally."
	>
		<span class="recapture__seg recapture__seg--basis" style="flex-basis: 30%">$600K</span>
		<span class="recapture__seg recapture__seg--recapture" style="flex-basis: 20%">$400K</span>
		<span class="recapture__seg recapture__seg--growth" style="flex-basis: 50%">$1,000,000</span>
	</div>

	<ul class="recapture__legend">
		<li>
			<span class="recapture__swatch recapture__swatch--basis"></span>
			<div>
				<strong>$600,000: your basis back.</strong>{' '}
				<span>Not taxed. This is the part of your investment you have not already deducted.</span>
			</div>
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="recapture__swatch recapture__swatch--recapture"></span>
			<div>
				<strong>$400,000: depreciation recapture.</strong>{' '}
				<span>The deductions you took come back as gain, taxed at up to 25% federally (at most $100,000).</span>
			</div>
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="recapture__swatch recapture__swatch--growth"></span>
			<div>
				<strong>$1,000,000: price growth.</strong>{' '}
				<span>Regular long-term capital gain, taxed at 0%, 15%, or 20% federally (at most $200,000).</span>
			</div>
		</li>
	</ul>

	<p class="recapture__note">
		Total taxable gain: $1,400,000. Federal figures only; the 3.8% net investment income tax may also apply, and California taxes the entire
		gain as ordinary income. A simplified illustration, not tax advice.
	</p>
</figure>

<style>
	.recapture {
		margin: 2rem 0;
		padding: 1.75rem;
		background: var(--paper-alt);
		border-top: 3px solid var(--gold);
		border-radius: 2px;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}

	.recapture__title {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		color: var(--navy-dark);
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}

	.recapture__steps {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.recapture__steps li {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		background: var(--paper);
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: 2px;
		padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
	}

	.recapture__step-label {
		color: var(--ink-light);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}

	.recapture__step-value {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1.35rem;
		color: var(--navy-dark);
	}

	.recapture__step-value--gold {
		color: var(--gold-dark);
	}

	.recapture__bar-label {
		margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.recapture__bar {
		display: flex;
		height: 46px;
		border-radius: 2px;
		overflow: hidden;
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}

	.recapture__seg {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}

	.recapture__seg--basis {
		background: var(--paper);
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		color: var(--ink-light);
	}

	.recapture__seg--recapture {
		background: var(--gold);
		color: var(--navy-dark);
	}

	.recapture__seg--growth {
		background: var(--navy);
		color: #fff;
	}

	.recapture__legend {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.recapture__legend li {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		align-items: flex-start;
	}

	.recapture__legend span:not(.recapture__swatch) {
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}

	.recapture__swatch {
		flex: none;
		width: 14px;
		height: 14px;
		margin-top: 0.3rem;
		border-radius: 3px;
	}

	.recapture__swatch--basis {
		background: var(--paper);
		border: 1px solid var(--ink-light);
	}

	.recapture__swatch--recapture {
		background: var(--gold);
	}

	.recapture__swatch--growth {
		background: var(--navy);
	}

	.recapture__note {
		margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		color: var(--ink-light);
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.recapture {
			padding: 1.25rem;
		}

		.recapture__steps {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
